  "solution": {
    "text": "Anypoint on the line is $(r+3,2 r+4,2 r+5)$. It lies on the plane $x+y+z=17$ $\\therefore(r+3)+(2 r+4)+(2 r+5)=17$ i.e $r=1$\r\n\r\nThus the point of intersection of the plane and the line is (4,6,7) Required distance $=$ distance between (3,4,5) and (4,6,7)\r\n\r\n$=\\sqrt{\\left\\{(4-3)^{2}+(6-4)^{2}+(7-5)^{2}\\right\\}}=3$",
